    <body>
      <div type="clause" n="49.1">
        <head><ref type="lawCode" target="law:Ine">Ine</ref> 49.1</head>
        <ab type="liebermannText" xml:lang="ang" source="#liebermann" n="49.1" corresp="#wit-e"><pb n="110" ed="#liebermann"/>Gif hie<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="20" target="#Ine_49-1.lnote.oe.20-2"/> þon<hi rend="italic">ne</hi> þær næren<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="21" target="#Ine_49-1.lnote.oe.21-2"/> oftor þon<hi rend="italic">ne</hi> æne, geselle<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="22" target="#Ine_49-1.lnote.oe.22-2"/> scill. se agenfrigea ⁊ gecyðe, þ<hi rend="italic">æt</hi> hie<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="20" target="#Ine_49-1.lnote.oe.20-2"/> þær oftor ne comen<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="23" target="#Ine_49-1.lnote.oe.23-2"/>, be þæs ceapes weorðe.<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="24" target="#Ine_49-1.lnote.oe.24-2"/></ab>
        <ab type="liebermannText" xml:lang="ang" source="#liebermann" n="49.1" corresp="#wit-h"><pb n="110" ed="#liebermann"/>Gif hi ðonne ðær næron oftor ðonne æne, gesylle<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="2" target="#Ine_49-1.lnote.oe.2"/> scilling se agenfriga ⁊ gecyðe, þæt hy<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="2" target="#Ine_49-1.lnote.oe.2"/> þær oftor næron, be ðæs ceapes wyrðe.<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="2" target="#Ine_49-1.lnote.oe.2"/></ab>
        <ab type="liebermannText" xml:lang="ang" source="#liebermann" n="49.1" corresp="#wit-b-no-prol"><pb n="110" ed="#liebermann"/>Gyf hi ðonne ðær næron oftor ðonne ǽne, gesylle<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="4" target="#Ine_49-1.lnote.oe.4"/> scilling se agenfríga ⁊ gecyðe, þ<hi rend="italic">æt</hi> hi ðær oftor ne comon, be ðæs ceapes wyrðe.</ab>
        <ab type="liebermannText" xml:lang="la" source="#liebermann" n="49.1" corresp="#wit-q"><pb n="111" ed="#liebermann"/>Si non fuerunt<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="20" target="#Ine_49-1.lnote.oe.20"/> ibi sepius quam semel, det agenfriga<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="21" target="#Ine_49-1.lnote.oe.21"/> (id<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="22" target="#Ine_49-1.lnote.oe.22"/> est liber cuius habentur) I<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="23" target="#Ine_49-1.lnote.oe.23"/> sol. et inueritet<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="24" target="#Ine_49-1.lnote.oe.24"/>, quod sepius non<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="25" target="#Ine_49-1.lnote.oe.25"/> fuerint<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="26" target="#Ine_49-1.lnote.oe.26"/> ibi, secundum ceapes<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="27" target="#Ine_49-1.lnote.oe.27"/> (captalis<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="28" target="#Ine_49-1.lnote.oe.28"/>) precium.</ab>
        <ab type="editionText" xml:lang="ang" source="#attenborough" corresp="#wit-e"><pb n="52" ed="#attenborough"/>Gif hie þonne þær næren<ptr type="editorNote" n="5" target="#Ine_49-1.attnote.fn.5"/> oftor þonne æne, geselle scill. se agenfrigea<ptr type="editorNote" n="6" target="#Ine_49-1.attnote.fn.6"/> ⁊ gecyðe, þæt hie þær oftor ne comen<ptr type="editorNote" n="7" target="#Ine_49-1.attnote.fn.7"/>, be þæs ceapes weorðe.</ab>
        <ab type="editionText" xml:lang="ang" source="#jurasinski-and-oliver" n="51.1" corresp="#wit-e"><pb n="412" ed="#jurasinski-and-oliver"/>Gif hie þon<hi rend="italic">ne</hi> þær næren oftor þon<hi rend="italic">ne</hi> æne, geselle sciƚƚ se agenfrigea ⁊ gecyðe, þ<hi rend="italic">æt</hi> hie þær oftor ne coman, be þæs ceapes weorðe.</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="de" source="#liebermann"><pb n="111" ed="#liebermann"/>Wenn sie nun nicht öfter als einmal dort waren, so gebe [ihm] der Eigenthümer<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="1" target="#Ine_49-1.lnote.de.1"/> [der Schweine einen] Schilling und beweise [durch Eid] in Höhe des Viehwerthes<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="2" target="#Ine_49-1.lnote.de.2"/>, dass sie nicht öfter dorthin gekommen<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="3" target="#Ine_49-1.lnote.de.3"/> seien.</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude" ana="#fromGerman">If they were not there more than once, let the owner [of the pigs] give [him one] shilling and prove [by an oath] to the amount of the value of the livestock that they did not come there more often.</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#attenborough" corresp="#wit-e"><pb n="53" ed="#attenborough"/>If, however, they have not been there more than once, the owner [of the swine] shall pay a shilling and declare [by an oath equivalent to the value of] the pigs<ptr type="editorNote" n="1" target="#Ine_49-1.attnote.n.1"/>, that they have not been there before.</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#whitelock"><pb n="405" ed="#whitelock"/>If, however, they were not there more often than once, the owner is to pay a shilling, and declare that they have not been there more often, by [an oath of) the value of the swine.</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#jurasinski-and-oliver" corresp="#wit-e"><pb n="413" ed="#jurasinski-and-oliver"/>If they were not there more than once, however, let the owner give a shilling and declare that they had not come more often, by [an oath equal to] the price of the livestock.</ab>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="Ine_49-1.lnote.oe.4" n="4" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">110</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de"><hi rend="spaced">ænne</hi> <hi rend="italic">im</hi> 16. <hi rend="italic">Jh. zugefügt</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude"><hi rend="italic">ænne</hi> added in the 16th cent.</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="Ine_49-1.lnote.oe.20" n="20" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">111</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">-rit <hi rend="italic">Lond;</hi> -rint <hi rend="italic">M Hk Br</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">-rit Lond; -rint M Hk Br</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="Ine_49-1.lnote.oe.21" n="21" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">111</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de"><hi rend="italic">fehlt Or</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">lacking in Or</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="Ine_49-1.lnote.oe.22" n="22" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">111</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">id — habentur <hi rend="italic">aus R T; fehlt Lond M Hk Br</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">id — habentur from R T; lacking in Lond M Hk Br</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="Ine_49-1.lnote.oe.23" n="23" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">111</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">sol. unum <hi rend="italic">Lond</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">sol. unum Lond</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="Ine_49-1.lnote.oe.24" n="24" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">111</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">monstret <hi rend="italic">Lond</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">monstret Lond</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="Ine_49-1.lnote.oe.25" n="25" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">111</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de"><hi rend="italic">fehlt K</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">lacking in K</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="Ine_49-1.lnote.oe.26" n="26" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">111</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">-runt <hi rend="italic">T</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">-runt T</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="Ine_49-1.lnote.oe.27" n="27" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">111</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de"><hi rend="italic">übergeschr. nur Co; fehlt übrigen</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">written above only in Co; lacking in the others</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="Ine_49-1.lnote.oe.28" n="28" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">111</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de"><hi rend="italic">so Lond;</hi> captale <hi rend="italic">übrige</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">thus Lond; captale the others</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="Ine_49-1.lnote.oe.2" n="2" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">110</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">y <hi rend="italic">auf Rasur</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">y on an erasure</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="Ine_49-1.lnote.oe.20-2" n="20" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">110</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">hi <hi rend="italic">Ld</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">hi Ld</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="Ine_49-1.lnote.oe.21-2" n="21" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">110</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">næron ofter <hi rend="italic">Ld</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">næron ofter Ld</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="Ine_49-1.lnote.oe.22-2" n="22" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">110</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">gesylle ænne sc. se agenfriga <hi rend="italic">Ld</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">gesylle ænne sc. se agenfriga Ld</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="Ine_49-1.lnote.oe.23-2" n="23" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">110</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">comon <hi rend="italic">Ld</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">comon Ld</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="Ine_49-1.lnote.oe.24-2" n="24" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">110</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">wyrþe <hi rend="italic">Ld</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">wyrþe Ld</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="erklaerung" xml:id="Ine_49-1.lnote.de.1" n="1" source="#liebermann-erkl"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">3</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">77</biblScope><biblScope unit="column">1</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">Q versteht das Wort (wie <hi rend="italic">o.</hi> 42, 1³) erst nicht, und dann nur halb durch silbenhaftes Übersetzen</seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">Q at first does not understand the word (as <hi rend="italic">above</hi> 42, 1³), and then only half, by translating it syllable by syllable</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="erklaerung" xml:id="Ine_49-1.lnote.de.2" n="2" source="#liebermann-erkl"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">3</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">77</biblScope><biblScope unit="column">1</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">der geschütteten 3 Schweine, also mit 6 Eideshufen; <hi rend="italic">s. d. Gl</hi> 2</seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">of the 3 impounded pigs, thus with 6 oath-hides; <hi rend="italic">see</hi> that word in <hi rend="italic">Gl</hi> 2</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="erklaerung" xml:id="Ine_49-1.lnote.de.3" n="3" source="#liebermann-erkl"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">3</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">77</biblScope><biblScope unit="column">1</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">‘dort waren’ H, aus 49, 2</seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">‘were there’ H, from 49, 2</seg></note>
        <note type="editorNote" subtype="footnote" xml:id="Ine_49-1.attnote.fn.5" n="5" source="#attenborough"><bibl><biblScope unit="page">52</biblScope></bibl><label>næren</label><seg type="original" xml:lang="en"><hi rend="italic">næron</hi>. B, H.</seg></note>
        <note type="editorNote" subtype="footnote" xml:id="Ine_49-1.attnote.fn.6" n="6" source="#attenborough"><bibl><biblScope unit="page">52</biblScope></bibl><label>agenfrigea</label><seg type="original" xml:lang="en"><hi rend="italic">agenfriga</hi>. B, H.</seg></note>
        <note type="editorNote" subtype="footnote" xml:id="Ine_49-1.attnote.fn.7" n="7" source="#attenborough"><bibl><biblScope unit="page">52</biblScope></bibl><label>comen</label><seg type="original" xml:lang="en"><hi rend="italic">oftor næron</hi>. H.</seg></note>
        <note type="editorNote" subtype="endnote" xml:id="Ine_49-1.attnote.n.1" n="1" source="#attenborough"><bibl><biblScope unit="page">190</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="en">For the value of a pig see VI As. cap. 6 § 2, <hi rend="italic">Duns.</hi> cap. 7.</seg></note>
      </div>
